# Exact process-identity translations used by exitlag-netd --identity-map.
# Format: SOURCE<TAB>WINDOWS_PATH (the separator must be one literal tab).
#
# SOURCE may be one of:
#   - the canonical absolute path from /proc/<pid>/exe, for a NATIVE Linux game;
#   - an exact .exe argv token, for a process that owns its own socket; or
#   - wineprefix:<absolute prefix dir>, matched against the WINEPREFIX of the
#     process owning the socket. This is the ONLY form that works for a Wine or
#     Proton game: at SYN time the socket is held by that prefix's wineserver,
#     whose /proc exe and argv are identical for every prefix on the machine.
#     It maps everything in that prefix to one identity, which is correct for
#     Proton (one prefix per title).
#
# Examples are commented out because nonexistent absolute sources intentionally
# fail startup. Copy this file and uncomment/edit only paths installed locally.
# native Linux game (source = /proc/<pid>/exe)
# /opt/my-native-game/bin/game	C:\Games\Supported Game\game.exe
# another Wine prefix
# wineprefix:/home/USER/prefixes/mygame	C:\Games\Supported Game\Game.exe
# Proton (one prefix per app id)
# wineprefix:/home/USER/.local/share/Steam/steamapps/compatdata/12345/pfx	C:\Games\Supported Game\Game.exe
